350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (The Reinforce & Release game is one of the most valuable exercises for any dog. It teaches a dog that staying close is always their choice, and that coming back is always worth it. The concept is simple: the dog is rewarded while remaining in contact, and then released with a clear signal. Through this pattern, the dog learns that holding focus leads to good things, and that every exercise has a clear beginning and end.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (This game builds duration, focus, and voluntary engagement without any pressure. The dog is never forced to stay; they choose to stay because the pattern makes sense and the outcome is consistently positive. It also strengthens a key part of the communication system: a reliable "keep going" marker that tells the dog they're on the right track, along with a self-initiated check-in and a default position that becomes second nature over time.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (Playing this game at the start of every session offers another benefit: it reveals, almost instantly, how easy or difficult a given environment is for the dog that day, making it one of the best ways to read a dog's state before moving on to other training. Over time, dogs who play this game regularly settle into focus more quickly, hold position with greater confidence, and wait for the release with calm anticipation rather than anxiety, building an engagement that travels easily into new and more challenging environments.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
