399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Place a treat between two fingers and your thumb so it is easy for your dog to notice and reach. When your dog makes their first attempt to get it, use your Static Confirmation marker and remove your thumb so they can access the treat.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Repeat a few times until your dog gains confidence in approaching your hand. Then, when they do, start using your Keep Going marker before the confirmation so that they understand they are doing well and that the treat will come soon.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Slowly start moving your hand slightly so they need to follow it and maintain contact with it while in motion, without having full access to the treat. After a small movement, use your Confirmation marker and release the treat.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Keep building duration in both hands until you can increase the difficulty by adding more steps, changing the tempo, and trying different directions and shapes.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (A few things to keep in mind)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (It is not enough for your dog to know how to follow each hand separately. They also need to learn how to transition between hands smoothly, without getting stuck on one side. Train that transition on its own before building a full luring flow.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (If your dog struggles to follow the lure, slow down and go back a few steps. Make the movement slower, shorter, and easier to follow. Create success before adding difficulty.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Luring is not a race. Every dog learns at their own pace, and our job is to make it as clear as possible from the very first moment.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [9]
>>
