/E (When rewarding, always deliver the treat from the opposite hand to the one your dog last looked at. If your dog looked at your right hand before giving up on the treat or looking at you, reward from your left, and vice versa. This keeps the exercise clean and prevents your dog from learning to simply look away from the hand that has the treat.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
